      "source": [
        "*Your answers here:*\n",
        "1. Nominal minus real is not equal to CPI growth because inflation and real growth combine multiplicatively. The identity is instead (1 + nominal growth) = (1 + real growth) x (1 + CPI growth). The number that represents inflation is the CPI's growth rate.\n",
        "\n",
        "2. PPP compares prices across countries by accounting for differences in currencies and price levels between countries. Deflation differs as it compares values across time by adjusting for changes in the price level within one country.\n",
        "\n",
        "3. The question I would ask is whether the 15% revenue growth is nominal or real after accounting for inflation. The real growth rate is (1.15 / 1.05) - 1 = about 9.5%."
